	m	(Lacq;IIIIIIIIIIII)V	a	method_48587	blitNineSliced
		c	Blits a nine-sliced portion of the texture specified by the atlas location onto the screen.\n<p>\n9-slicing is a 2D technique which allows you to reuse an image at various sizes without needing to prepare multiple assets.\nIt involves splitting the image into nine portions, so that when you re-size the sprite, the different portions scale or tile (that is, repeat in a grid formation) in different ways to keep the sprite in proportion.\n<p>\nThis is useful when creating patterns or textures, such as walls or floors in a 2D environment.\n<p>\nThis method is mainly used for GUI and Button rendering, to create scaleable/tileable assets.
		p	1			atlasLocation
			c	the location of the texture atlas.
		p	2			x
			c	the x-coordinate of the top-left corner of the target position.
		p	3			y
			c	the y-coordinate of the top-left corner of the target position.
		p	4			width
			c	the width of the target portion.
		p	5			height
			c	the height of the target portion.
		p	6			leftSliceWidth
			c	the width of the left column's slices.
		p	7			topSliceHeight
			c	the height of the top row's slices.
		p	8			rightSliceWidth
			c	the width of the right column's slices.
		p	9			bottomSliceHeight
			c	the height of the bottom row's slices.
		p	10			uWidth
			c	the width of the source texture.
		p	11			vHeight
			c	the height of the source texture.
		p	12			textureX
			c	the x-coordinate of the top-left corner of the source.
		p	13			textureY
			c	the y-coordinate of the top-left corner of the source.
